Product-designer's regression review of the stage-4 screens found no regressions and one new non-blocking finding, D13. The report is at `work/reviews/design-16fff73.md`.

The screen code is byte-identical to stage 3. On the stage-4 build, at phone and desktop widths, they confirmed:
- no page scrolls sideways;
- labels, keyboard focus and contrast are unchanged;
- the seven required states still look different;
- the twelve earlier screen fixes still hold.

**D13:** a refund shows up in the activity feed looking exactly like an ordinary new payment. Refunding 5.00 EUR of a "Pizza Friday" payment shows a plain "paid ada, 5.00 EUR, Sent, Pizza Friday" row. That weakens stage 2's rule that money movement should be understandable at a glance. They added a fix to the design direction (`work/design.md` §5.3): refund rows say "Refund sent" or "Refund received" and carry a return-arrow icon, with every required element unchanged.

I'll send D13 to implementer with the rest of round 1's findings. Round 1 is still waiting on test-designer's acceptance check and reviewer's code review.

